# gameStart
@back bg_black

@set left="15,-90"
@set leftmid="25,-90"
@set mid="50,-90"
@set rightmid="75,-90"
@set right="85,-90"
@set afetoTiradentes=0
@set afetoHipolita=0
@set afetoBarbara=0
@set afetoJoaquim=0
@set afetoCel=0
@set liberaBarbara=false
@set liberaCelio=false
@set liberaHipolita=false
@set liberaJoaquim=false
@set liberaTiradentes=false
@set demoVersion=false

; Rota Comum
; Cena Start - Escolha
@back bg_black
NA: Choose your appearance.
@char PLAYERF.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
@char PLAYERM.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
@choice Left goto:.female
@choice Right goto:.male
@stop

# female
@set gender="female"
@set PLAYER="PLAYERF"
@set name="Maria"
@set selector=0
@hideChars
@goto .scene0-0
# male
@set gender="male"
@set PLAYER="PLAYERM"
@set name="João"
@set selector=1
@hideChars
@goto .scene0-0




; Cena 0.0 — O tempo se rompe
# scene0-0
NA: Choose your name.
@input name summary:"Choose your name."
@stop

;@choice Tiradentes goto:rota_tiradentes
;@choice Hipolita goto:rota_hipolita
;@choice Joaquim goto:rota_joaquim
;@choice Barbara goto:rota_barbara
;@choice Cel goto:rota_cel
;@choice Comum
;@stop

@bgm backInTime volume:0.7

;NA: “They say the mountains of Minas keep secrets."
NA: “They say the mountains of Minas keep secrets."
NA: "Secrets buried beneath gold, blood, and promises…"
NA: "But some promises refuse to stay buried."
NA: "They pull. They call."
NA: "They refuse silence.”
; @fadeout 1
@gosub .BlackScreen

; Scene 1
@wait 1.0

; AAA
@back bg_farm.Crossfade pos:70,100 scale:2.0 time:0 wait!
@slide MainBackground to:70,90
NA: Down there, under the scorching sun and the dry soil of Minas Gerais, you slowly wake up in a time that does not belong to you.

; Variação de gênero
@if gender="female"
NA: Wearing tailored pants and a band T-shirt. Slowly, you begin to move, little by little.
@endif
@if gender="male"
NA: Wearing jeans and your sweater over your shirt. Slowly, you begin to move, little by little.
@endif
@stopBgm fade:5 !wait

NA: Your eyes blink a few times, absorbing the brightness hitting your pupils. Your body feels hot, and your head seems to throb.
PLAYER: Where am I?
NA: With difficulty and exhaustion, you slowly sit up. Dust falls from your clothes as you try to stand.
PLAYER: I was…..
NA: Confusion lingers in your mind, your memories are tangled and mixed together.
PLAYER: I remember being there, and then a flash of light… now I’m here.
@hide MainBackground
@back bg_farm.Crossfade pos:50,50 scale:1.0 time:1.5 wait!

@char {PLAYER}.surprise look:left pos:{mid}
@bgm wander volume:0.7

NA: You look around, feeling the weight of the sun.
PLAYER: Here where? And what kind of hellish heat is this…
NA: From afar, you hear something striking the ground with force. A sound you can’t recognize, but it seems to be approaching fast.
@sfx horse !wait
NA: When you turn around, you come face to face with horses and several wagons approaching.
PLAYER: But what the—
; AQUI: PULAR PRA TRAS
@slide {PLAYER} to:50,-85 easing:easeOutElastic time:0.5
@slide {PLAYER} to:{mid} time:0.3
NA: Just in time, you awkwardly jump backward, barely avoiding being hit.
MERCHANT: Don’t you watch where you’re going?
@stopSfx fade:3 !wait
@char {PLAYER}.thinking

PLAYER: Sorry, it’s not like I was standing in the middle of the street.
NA: The merchant passes slowly, staring at you with a curious expression. He looks at you in shock and clearly doesn’t understand anything you’re saying.
MERCHANT: This fellow talks crooked… not from around here.
PLAYER: Great. I time-traveled just to become a circus attraction.
NA: They move on with their horses and wagons, leaving you even more confused than before.
PLAYER: Wagons and horses? What is this, the Middle Ages?
NA: Looking around, you notice you’re wearing only one sneaker, and your phone is shattered inside your pocket.
PLAYER: Great. If only I could get a signal… signal—what am I thinking?
@sfx horse !wait
NA: New sounds of horses trotting closer make you take a few hesitant steps back.
NA: Riders pass by, wearing odd clothes and apparently carrying weapons. They look at you with disdain.
NA: One of them throws a provocation your way.
SOLDIER: You dress like a fairground fool.
@sfx risada volume:0.3
NA: They all seem to laugh as they hurry past, while you simply clench your fists in response.
@stopSfx fade:3 !wait
PLAYER: Now I’m being insulted by people dressed like museum exhibits.

@char {PLAYER}.neutral look:left pos:{mid}

PLAYER: Let’s assume this isn’t a dream or some messed-up coma. That means the machine worked, and I’m...?
PLAYER: This doesn’t look like a setting from any of the great wars. If I can find… or at least manage to talk to someone.
PLAYER: Maybe I should go that way. I’ve seen wagons and soldiers—what else could there be?
NA: You turn slightly, as if expecting an answer that never comes.

@char {PLAYER}.determined look:left pos:{mid}

NA: Yeah, keep talking to yourself… that doesn’t look strange at all.

; Scene 2

NA: With one foot wearing a shoe and the other only in a rather funny sock, you start walking in the same direction the horses and wagons went. The dry stone ground and the sun feel like pure torture.
NA: Along the way, after thinking about giving up and sitting down more than once.
NA: The sound of a softer trot draws your attention again.

@char {PLAYER}.neutral look:left pos:{mid}

PLAYER: Yeah… this really is a busy road.
NA: When you look back, you see a man of average build approaching on horseback. Unlike the others, he slows down when he notices you.

@char {PLAYER}.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}

NA: He pulls the reins and brings the horse to a stop beside you.
NA: The man looks you up and down — the strange clothes, the lost posture, the confused gaze.
@char AL.smile look:left pos:{leftmid}

NA: A half-smile appears on his face, more curious than hostile.
??: One does not often see folk dressed like that in these parts.
NA: He tilts his head, clearly sizing you up.
??: Lost your convoy… or did you fall from the sky?

@char {PLAYER}.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: From the con— the what?
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
NA: He raises an eyebrow, staring at you.
@char {PLAYER}.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: Let’s just say I woke up in the wrong place.
NA: With an amused smile on his lips, he says:
@char AL.smile look:left pos:{leftmid}
??: That happens. But folk usually wake in a bed, not on a road.
PLAYER: You’re right… where are we?
??: In Vila Rica — or at least on the road leading to it.
@char {PLAYER}.surprise look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: Vila Rica?
@char AL.surprise look:left pos:{leftmid}
???: Don’t tell me you didn’t know where you were stepping?
@char {PLAYER}.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: I had absolutely no idea.
NA: He arches an eyebrow, watching you closely.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
??: You speak in a peculiar way… and those clothes are not from around here, that much is certain.
NA: He nudges the horse forward at a slow pace, still observing you.
??: And so, where do you come from?
@char {PLAYER}.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: São Paulo.
@char AL.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
NA: The man furrows his brow, thoughtful.
??: The Captaincy of São Paulo?
@char {PLAYER}.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: If you say so… then I suppose it is.
NA: He studies you more carefully now, as if sensing something strange, but chooses not to press.
@char AL.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
??: Then you truly came from far away. That explains quite a lot.
NA: A brief silence settles between you, until he lets out a half-smile.
??: Wherever you may be from, it seems the road has betrayed you.
NA: He adjusts himself in the saddle and extends his hand.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
??: My name is Inácio José de Alvarenga Peixoto, but you may call me Alvarenga.
@char {PLAYER}.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: It’s a pleasure.
AL: And you, what is your name?
PLAYER: My name is {name}. Bureaucracy shortened names over time.
NA: For a moment, Alvarenga falls silent, studying you closely.
NA: He presses his lips together, as if deciding whether to ask or not.
@char AL.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: Bureaucracy…?
NA: The word sounds odd on his tongue. He lets out a brief, restrained laugh — more curious than suspicious.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: Be that as it may, your name is far too short for this land… and your manner confirms the rest.
NA: Alvarenga gently pulls the reins, turning the horse back toward the main road.
@char AL.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: Very well, {name}. Wherever you came from, it’s not wise to linger here.
NA: Alvarenga moves the horse forward at a slow pace, riding alongside you.
NA: Silence stretches for a few steps, until you can’t take it anymore.
PLAYER: Why are you helping me?
NA: He looks ahead, thoughtful.
@char AL.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: Because those who wander lost tend to cause trouble.
NA: He throws you a quick glance.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: And you don’t seem dangerous. Just… out of place.
NA: You frown.
@char {PLAYER}.surprise look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: And that’s enough?
NA: Alvarenga gives a half-smile.
@char AL.smile look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: Also because I was once lost… and someone extended a hand to me.
NA: He nods toward the road ahead.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: Besides, Vila Rica is full of watchful eyes. A lone stranger draws far too much attention.
NA: As you walk along the road, Alvarenga glances again at your clothes, assessing.
AL: Those garments attract far too much attention.
NA: He hesitates for a moment, as if weighing his own generosity.

; Variação de gênero
; Se o jogador for homem
@if gender="male"
AL: I can lend you some clothes. They’re not new, but at least they don’t look like they came from a trinket stall.
NA: You look at him, a little surprised.
@char {PLAYER}.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
PLAYER: I’ll return them.
NA: Alvarenga smiles faintly.
@char AL.happy look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: I certainly hope so. I don’t look nearly as elegant without them.
@endif

; Se o jogador for mulher
@if gender="female"
@char AL.shy look:left pos:{leftmid}
AL: My wife may have something that fits you.
NA: He says it, a bit embarrassed.
AL: She’s curious. She’ll likely have questions.
@endif
