PLAYER: They say many things… your work as a dentist, your role in the Minas conspiracy, and about your…
NA: You hesitate, remembering the fate history books gave Tiradentes.
NA: He notices the pause and tilts his head slightly, understanding.
@char TI.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Do not trouble yourself. I would rather be remembered poorly than not remembered at all.
PLAYER: Right…
NA: You glance around, trying to change the subject.
PLAYER: The words you spoke were beautiful… but dangerous.
NA: Tiradentes lets out a tired, knowing half-smile.
TI: Speeches always sound better from a distance, don’t they?

@choice "People really listened" goto:.scene1T-1
@choice "Words don’t fill empty stomachs" goto:.scene1T-2
@stop

# scene1T-1
@set liberaTiradentes=true
NA: Tiradentes studies you for a longer moment.
@char TI.smile look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: I like the way you think.
TI: If there were time and occasion… much more could be said.
NA: A guard passes not far away.
NA: Tiradentes notices immediately. He lowers his voice — cautious, not conspiratorial.
@char TI.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Vila Rica is full of attentive ears.
TI: Choose carefully what you carry with you.
NA: He takes two steps away, then pauses.
@char TI.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Still…
TI: Not every silence is a virtue.

@goto .scene1T-3end

# scene1T-2
NA: He breathes deeply, as if deciding not to argue with the world.
@char TI.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: I know hunger.
TI: I know the weight of taxes, of gold vanishing from empty hands at day’s end.
NA: A brief, weary smile.
@char TI.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: If words don’t fill stomachs… at least they remind us they exist.
NA: He nods to you with respect.
NA: You look back thoughtfully, wondering whether your words can truly help him.
@choice "Maybe I want to hear more" goto:.scene1T-1
@choice "It’s none of my concern" goto:.scene1T-3
@stop


# scene1T-3
@set liberaTiradentes=false
NA: Tiradentes’ gaze darkens slightly.
@char TI.angry look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: For one who comes from afar, I understand.
TI: The troubles of this town may not reach you.
PLAYER: I didn’t say that.
PLAYER: I just think words can bring serious consequences.
@char TI.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: And silence brings them as well.
NA: He gives a short nod.
TI: Farewell.
NA: Without waiting for a reply, he disappears into the crowd.
@goto .TESTE
@goto .scene1T-3end


# scene1T-3end

; Depois das escolhas
; CENA 5
@hideChars
NA: Tiradentes melts back into the crowd.
@stopBgm fade:3 !wait
NA: The square returns to its usual noise — vendors calling out, footsteps, distant bells.
@bgm wander volume:0.7
NA: The soldiers remain watchful, and Alvarenga returns to your side.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{mid}
AL: It would be wise for us to move along.
AL: Not everyone appreciates seeing authority challenged in public.
NA: You agree.
NA: But as you walk, one thing remains clear: the books you read
NA: do not do justice to the man you just met.
NA: Alvarenga leads you into a quieter street, away from the square’s bustle. The voices fade behind you, replaced by the distant creak of wagons and hurried footsteps.
NA: He stops near a calmer stretch of road, shaded by nearby buildings.
AL: Here you are safer. It would not be wise to wander much for now.
NA: You look at him, intrigued.
NA: He seems restless, glancing back.
PLAYER: Are you going back to the square?
AL: Alvarenga hesitates for a moment, choosing his words.
@char AL.thinking look:left pos:{mid}
AL: I need to speak with a friend… and look into a certain matter.
NA: There is something incomplete in the way he says it — as if there were a name he prefers not to mention.
PLAYER: Sounds important.
NA: He inclines his head slightly.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{mid}
AL: In Vila Rica, almost everything is.
NA: He mounts his horse again, takes the reins, and before leaving, gives you one last warning:
AL: Wait here.
AL: And if you do decide to walk… do not stray too far.
@hideChars
NA: With that, he rides off down the dirt road, blending back into the city.
NA: You are left alone.
NA: The sun still weighs heavy overhead, and Vila Rica pulses around you.
NA: You take a deep breath.

