# scene6
@stopBgm fade:5 !wait
@back bg_squareAfternoon.Crossfade time:1.5 wait!
NA: You and Alvarenga return to the town square after walking for some time.
NA: You pass by soldiers who have resumed their watch following Tiradentes’ speech.
NA: The soldiers exchange looks — clearly displeased — but step back.
@bgm tension volume:0.7
NA: A Crown officer with rigid posture gives you a long, measuring stare, as if committing your face to memory.
NA: He turns away, his cloak swaying behind him.
NA: Alvarenga approaches immediately, resting a firm but subtle hand on your arm.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{mid}
AL: Come. Before they change their minds.
NA: You move away together, blending once more into the square’s crowd.
NA: The murmur slowly returns — but it no longer sounds the same.
NA: In the distance, you spot Tiradentes speaking with a few men. Alert, he briefly meets your gaze.
NA: This time he does not smile. He simply inclines his head.
NA: Across the square, Joaquim watches the scene while leaning against a column, his expression hard to read. When he notices you looking, he raises an eyebrow slightly.
NA: You feel eyes on you.
NA: One step. Then another.
NA: As you try to move away, a voice cuts through the air.
SOLDIER: You there. A moment.
NA: Two soldiers approach, hands near their weapons — not aggressive, but clearly suspicious.
SOLDIER: You’ve been observing too closely.
SOLDIER: Writing anything down, by chance?
PLAYER: I wasn’t doing anything.
NA: One soldier exchanges a glance with the other.

SOLDIER: They all say that.
NA: Alvarenga, who was nearby, notices the situation and steps back toward you — but another soldier raises a hand to stop him.
NA: Stay where you are, sir.
NA: Tell us — whom do you serve?
PLAYER: No one. I just… arrived in the city.
NA: A short, uncomfortable silence.
SOLDIER: Just… arrived.
NA: The tone makes it clear this does not help.

NA: You speak too quickly. Your words sound strange.
NA: The soldiers frown, hands tightening near their weapons.
SOLDIER: Your speech is… crooked.
SOLDIER: Doesn’t sound like a mule driver or a miner.
NA: Another soldier folds his arms.
SOLDIER: And that’s usually a bad sign.
NA: Ignoring the warning, Alvarenga steps forward, placing himself between you and the men.
AL: That’s enough, gentlemen.
AL: The disturbance is over. There’s no crime here.
NA: The captain watches him with a cold smile — almost satisfied.
CAPTAIN: You never tire of standing where you shouldn’t… do you?
NA: He circles Alvarenga slowly, assessing him.
CAPTAIN: First… certain poorly explained dealings in your household.
CAPTAIN: Then your persistent protection of the alferes. 
CAPTAIN: Now this stranger who appears from nowhere… and listens too closely.
NA: The captain’s gaze slides toward you.
CAPTAIN: You do seem fond of collecting trouble, Mr. Alvarenga.
NA: Alvarenga’s jaw tightens. His voice comes out steady — loaded with tension.
@char AL.angry look:left pos:{mid}
AL: I attend to what is my duty.
AL: And I owe no explanation of hospitality to those who mistake surveillance for justice.
NA: One of the soldiers lets out a low laugh.
SOLDIER: Still believe name and coin solve everything?
NA: The captain raises a hand for silence, though his tone remains provocative.
CAPTAIN: The Crown’s power does not bend to favors.
CAPTAIN: Nor to gold… nor to good company.

NA: Alvarenga exhales an ironic sigh, almost disbelieving what he just heard. He steps forward, anger finally surfacing.
@char AL.determined look:left pos:{mid}
AL: Do not invoke virtue while you feed on another man’s suffering.
AL: If there is disorder in Vila Rica, it is born of blind exaction.
NA: Silence grows heavy.
NA: For a moment, you think this has gone too far.
NA: The captain merely smiles — slow and deliberate.
CAPTAIN: Dangerous words.
CAPTAIN: You walk far too close to the alferes, sir.
NA: He turns to the soldiers.
CAPTAIN: Mark this outsider’s face well.
CAPTAIN: Do not lose sight of him.
NA: His gaze returns to Alvarenga.
CAPTAIN: Today, we shall let it pass.
CAPTAIN: Tomorrow… we shall see if your influence weighs as much as you believe.
NA: He makes as if to leave.
NA: The air seems to relax — for a single second.
NA: Then the sound of firm footsteps cuts through the murmur. A strange silence spreads across the square.
NA: A man of imposing stature emerges among the soldiers — immaculate attire, a cold and calculating gaze.
NA: He does not need to announce himself.
NA: The soldiers straighten immediately.
@char AL.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}

@char VI.angry look:left pos:{leftmid}

??: What a fine spectacle you’ve arranged here.

NA: The captain swallows hard.
CAPTAIN: Viscount… it was merely—
VI: Merely?
NA: His gaze sweeps the area slowly.
VI: An alferes stirring the people in a public square. Performers mocking the Crown.
VI: And now… yet another stranger in the midst of chaos.
NA: His eyes settle on Alvarenga.
VI: And, as always, you at the center of the disturbance.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
NA: Alvarenga steps forward, striving to maintain dignity.
AL: Viscount, there is no disorder that—

@char VI.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}

VI: Silence.
NA: The interruption is sharp and abrupt.
NA: Two soldiers step closer to Alvarenga — just enough to remind him he holds no power here.
NA: The Viscount then turns to you. His gaze is heavy, cold, and assessing.
VI: And who is this now?
VI: For what reason were you listening to what does not concern you?
NA: Alvarenga attempts to intervene.
@char AL.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
@if gender="female"
AL: She is under my—
@else
AL: He is under my—
@endif
VI: I did not address you.
NA: Silence weighs on the air. Alvarenga’s jaw tightens in clear irritation, while the Viscount simply ignores him, focusing on you.

@if gender="female"
NA: The viscount frowns.
@char VI.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: A woman… alone?
VI: And tell me—under whose care are you?
NA: His tone is not concerned. It is interrogative.
VI: Or do ladies now wander unaccompanied among soldiers and agitators?
NA: An uneasy murmur spreads through the crowd. He studies you from head to toe, measuring.
PLAYER: I… uh…
VI: Where is your husband? Or your father? A guardian, at the very least?
PLAYER: I have none.
NA: That answer stirs even more murmurs.
VI: That is most improper.
VI: A woman without protection is trouble… or makes it.
NA: His patronizing tone irritates you. Your fists clench until your knuckles turn white as you glare back at him.
SOLDIER: We cannot simply let her wander like this.
SOLDIER: She will be placed under the supervision of someone respectable.
NA: You feel the weight of the word *placed*.
@endif

@if gender="male"
@char VI.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
NA: The viscount raises an eyebrow slightly.
NA: A man with no known trade, no master, no clear purpose…
NA: He tilts his head, assessing you.
@char VI.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: Some would call that a traveler.
VI: I usually call it a vagrant.
NA: A cold smile curls on his lips.
VI: Or worse… an accomplice.
@endif

NA: His gaze slides briefly toward Alvarenga.
@char VI.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: You seem to have a curious taste for troublesome company.
VI: I wonder what advantage a married man finds… in surrounding himself with such inconvenient companions.
NA: His eyes move from you to Alvarenga, heavy with judgment.
@wait 0.4
NA: Before the tension can erupt, a familiar voice cuts through the silence.
@hide AL
@char TI.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Your Excellency.
NA: He approaches with a firm but respectful posture.
@char TI.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: I see no crime here that would justify such diligence.
NA: The viscount smiles without humor.
@char VI.smile look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: Alferes.
VI: Your boldness today has exceeded what is tolerable.
NA: His gaze shifts to someone approaching.
NA: Joaquim appears shortly after, his expression far too relaxed for the situation.
@char JO.neutral look:left pos:{mid}
NA: Tiradentes keeps his posture straight.
TI: I merely reminded the crowd that the square is not a barracks, Your Excellency.
NA: A soldier steps forward, but the viscount raises a hand, stopping him.
@char VI.angry look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: A reminder?
VI: You call it a reminder to stir murmurs against the Crown?
NA: He steps a little closer.
VI: You spoke of taxes, of gold, of burdens…
VI: Dangerous words, spoken into the wrong ears.
NA: Tiradentes holds his gaze.
TI: I spoke only what all feel and few dare to say.
NA: The viscount lets out a short, bitter laugh.
@char VI.smile look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: Courage you do not lack.
VI: Judgment, perhaps.
NA: His attention turns to Joaquim.
@char VI.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: And you, Reis…
VI: I see you hurry to defend the alferes.
@char JO.thinking look:left pos:{mid}
JO: Well… if you question everyone who listens to a speech, the square will soon be empty.
@char TI.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: This person was with me earlier.
TI: Nothing more than curiosity… a virtue still permitted, I believe.
NA: He inclines his head slightly.
@char VI.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: Two uniformed men protecting an inconvenient speech…
VI: This foreigner—and these words—must be of great importance indeed.
NA: Joaquim answers with an easy smile, though his tone is firm.
@char JO.smile look:left pos:{mid}
JO: Vila Rica has grown rather small of late, Your Excellency.
JO: We keep running into the same faces… and the same problems.
NA: The viscount examines him from head to toe.
@char VI.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: Reis…
NA: A calculated pause.
VI: Still playing at being a great merchant?
NA: He steps forward.
@char VI.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: Tell me—do you come here as a man of business…
VI: Or as a soldier who seems to have forgotten to whom he owes obedience?
NA: Joaquim keeps smiling, but his eyes harden.
JO: I serve the Crown when it serves order. Not abuse.
NA: A restless murmur spreads through the square.
NA: The viscount’s expression darkens.
VI: Your manners grow dangerously loose, Reis.
NA: He casts one last glance at Tiradentes.
@char VI.angry look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: And your speeches gather far too many listeners, Alferes
NA: Silence.
NA: The viscount steps back, reclaiming control.
@char VI.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: Not today.
NA: He gestures briefly to the soldiers.
VI: But do not mistake my patience for forgetfulness.
NA: His eyes turn to you again.
NA: Once more, the question—now almost a sentence.
@char VI.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
VI: So then…
VI: Under whose protection are you?


NA: Silence falls like a weight.
