CE: Then you understand a little of what I mean.
NA: He gestures broadly toward the stage, where puppets and scenery await the next show.
CE: Theater doesn’t change the world.
CE: But for an hour, it lets Vila Rica forget the weight of gold… debts… and the names that watch us.
NA: His voice lowers slightly.
CE: Here, people laugh.
CE: And those who laugh… breathe.
NA: You nod without quite realizing.
@char {PLAYER}2.neutral look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: Makes sense.
PLAYER: Sometimes that’s all you can do.
NA: You hesitate, then add — almost teasing:
@char {PLAYER}2.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: But provoking the Crown in public helps with what, exactly?
PLAYER: Besides earning yourself a death sentence, you sound almost as reckless as Tiradentes.
NA: Célio stops walking.
NA: He doesn’t seem offended — only attentive.
NA: He studies the empty stage for a moment before answering.
@char CE.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Madness… is a light word, spoken by those who’ve never felt their chest tighten.
NA: He turns to you, voice calm but firm.
CE: The alferes doesn’t raise his voice because he ignores danger.
CE: He does it because he knows it better than most who fear it.
NA: A crooked smile crosses his face, edged with irony.
CE: The Crown treasures silence.
CE: Silence asks no questions… and leaves no memory.
NA: He takes two steps forward, as if rehearsing an invisible speech.
CE: Theater does the same — by other means.
CE: Where he shouts, I raise puppets. Where he speaks of taxes, I show hunger… disguised as laughter.
NA: You cross your arms, thoughtful.
@char {PLAYER}2.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: Still… it feels small against armed men.
NA: Célio lets out a low laugh, humorless.
@char CE.smile look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Swords wound the flesh.
CE: Ideas… take longer. But they never ask permission.
NA: He leans in slightly, as if sharing something precious.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: The square forgets quickly.
CE: The stage doesn’t. Those who laugh today… think tomorrow.
NA: A brief pause.
CE: If that’s madness… then Vila Rica is full of madmen who learned to stay quiet for too long.
NA: He studies you again, renewed curiosity in his eyes.
@char CE.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: And you?
CE: You speak like someone who doubts… but doesn’t look away.
NA: There’s something sincere in his gaze — curiosity mixed with challenge.
@char {PLAYER}2.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: I understand protesting authority.
PLAYER: I’ve been to demonstrations, questioned plenty… but here… in this backward place, everything feels riskier.
PLAYER: Death could be decided by someone in a ridiculous wig back in Portugal saying, “well then.”
NA: Célio bursts into laughter — loud, genuine, impossible to contain.
@char CE.happy look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: By the saints…
CE: I’ve never heard Lisbon described so accurately.
NA: He wipes at his face, still smiling.
@char CE.smile look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: You’re certainly not from around here — no doubt about that.
CE: You speak like someone who’s traveled far… and still looks at things with unburdened eyes.
NA: The laughter fades into something more attentive.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Strange… and singular.
CE: Vila Rica hasn’t offered me novelty like this in quite some time.
NA: He watches you carefully now.
NA: Curiosity settles in his gaze — sincere, edged with challenge.
@char CE.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Tell me honestly.
CE: Have you ever felt the urge to say something… even knowing you shouldn’t?
@char {PLAYER}2.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: All the time.
NA: The distant sounds of the city return — hurried footsteps, voices, clanking metal.
NA: Célio’s tone softens, almost playful.
@char CE.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Perhaps that’s why you lingered here.
CE: Theater has a way of recognizing those burdened with too many questions. So then… if it doesn’t trouble you…
NA: He steps a little closer, voice more personal now.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: I’d like you to watch one of our rehearsals.
CE: Not a performance for crowds… only for those who know how to look.
NA: A brief pause, thick with expectation.
CE: What do you say?

@choice Refuse goto:.scene2C-1
@choice Accept goto:.scene2C-2
@stop

# scene2C-1
@char {PLAYER}2.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: I think I’d better not. I’m still trying to understand this place.
NA: He accepts the answer with quiet grace.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: I understand. A city does not reveal itself to those in a hurry.
NA: A faint smile.
CE: But the curtains remain open… should you change your mind.
@stopBgm fade:3 !wait
@gosub .BlackScreen
@goto .scene1C-2end
