# scene2C-2
@set liberaCelio=true
@char {PLAYER}2.smile look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: I’d like that. Truly.
NA: Célio smiles, pleased.
@char CE.smile look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Then come.
CE: Perhaps the stage has something to teach you as well.
NA: As you properly step into the theater—
NA: The wooden benches creak under the weight of silence. The scent of old fabric, paint, and wax hangs thick in the air.
NA: Célio lights a few candles onstage. Shadows stretch along the walls, warped and alive.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Pay no mind to the bareness of the place.
CE: A stage without an audience is like a square without rumor… it seems dead, but merely sleeps.
NA: He moves naturally among puppets and costumes.
NA: On a nearby table lie wooden figures with exaggerated faces: a long-nosed tax collector, a bent miner, a weary-eyed woman.
@char {PLAYER}2.surprise look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: These actually go on stage?
NA: Célio smiles, almost proud.
@char CE.smile look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: They do.
CE: And under laughter — the only blade that slips by unnoticed.
NA: He lifts the tax collector puppet.
CE: <i>“Pay, pay… for even the air you breathe belongs to His Majesty.”</i>
NA: The miner puppet answers, hunched:
@char CE.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: “Then take my breath as well… for gold I have no more.”
NA: Célio lowers the puppets, watching your reaction.
@char CE.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: You see?
CE: I don’t say “Crown.” I don’t say “Portugal”… yet those who listen understand.
@char {PLAYER}2.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: That’s… surprisingly direct.
NA: Célio tilts his head, measuring the words.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Too direct, and doors close.
CE: Veiled… and people laugh, carry it home… and think later.
NA: He steps closer to the stage and sits on its edge.
CE: Theater doesn’t change the world in a night.
NA: A brief pause.
NA: Célio rises and wipes his hands on a cloth.
@char CE.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: This city distrusts those without ties.
CE: No name, no home, no trade… suspicion comes swiftly.
NA: He glances around, then back to you, more serious now.
@char CE.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: If anyone asks…
CE: You’ll say you assist me here. Rehearsals, backstage work — whatever is needed.
@char {PLAYER}2.happy look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: Are you offering me a job?
NA: Célio lets out a short laugh.
@char CE.smile look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: An honest pretext is sometimes all that keeps someone safe in these streets.
NA: He steps a little closer, lowering his voice.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{mid}
CE: I ask for no oath, no banner.
CE: Only attentive eyes… and silence when it’s wise.
NA: A measured pause.
@char CE.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Do you accept?
@char {PLAYER}2.smile look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: Sure. I have a feeling I’m going to like it here.
NA: Célio nods, satisfied.
@char CE.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
CE: Then you stand under my roof… at least in words.
CE: And in Vila Rica, words carry more weight than they should.
@gosub .BlackScreen


# scene1C-2end

; Cena C3 - Encontro com Alvarenga
@back bg_squareDay.Crossfade time:1.5 wait!
NA: As you leave the theater, the late-afternoon air feels cooler.
NA: The city murmurs — hurried footsteps, hushed voices, distant bells.
NA: At the doorway, Alvarenga waits, leaning against the wall with arms crossed.
AL: I see you’ve chosen… interesting company.
@char {PLAYER}2.surprise look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: Were you waiting for me?
NA: Alvarenga exhales, half resigned.
@char AL.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
AL: Let’s say I’ve learned not to lose sight of those who attract too many eyes.
AL: Especially the Crown’s.
NA: He casts a quick glance at the theater.
@char AL.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
AL: Artists like him… tend to draw unwanted attention.
@char {PLAYER}2.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: He’s just putting on a play.
NA: Alvarenga raises a brow.
@char AL.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
AL: Around here, “just” rarely means little.
NA: A heavy silence settles.
@char AL.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
AL: I’m not saying you chose poorly.
AL: Only… be cautious.
NA: He pushes off the wall, gesturing down the street.
AL: Come.
NA: Together, you head back along the stone streets.
